{"id": "cma-132850", "status": "ok", "meta": "Plums from Hampton Court's gardens in Pomona Britannica, George Brookshaw's 1806 book of English fruit, with the dark aquatint ground.", "about": "Plums from the gardens at Hampton Court Palace fill this plate from Pomona Britannica, George Brookshaw's big book of English fruit. The museum says those gardens were the most celebrated around London, and that the book was devoted to the handsomest varieties grown in England. Most of its 90 plates, like this one, were printed with dark aquatint backgrounds.", "museum_record": "https://clevelandart.org/art/1955.310", "inventory_number": "", "dimensions": "", "credit_line": "", "sources": ["https://clevelandart.org/art/1955.310", "https://artnap.com/artwork/cma-132850"], "check": "clean"}
