{"id": "aic-80499", "status": "ok", "meta": "Two girls in a dancing lesson: Cecilia Beaux's 1898 double portrait of the daughters of her friends Helena de Kay and Richard Watson Gilder.", "about": "Two girls move through a dancing lesson in Cecilia Beaux's double portrait of the daughters of her friends Helena de Kay and Richard Watson Gilder. The museum says the picture cares less about who the sitters are than about how they move together, and that it catches the shift from girlhood to adolescence. Beaux was competing for portrait commissions in a market dominated by men, and the museum says she did very well. She was also the first woman to win a faculty post at the Pennsylvania Academy of the Fine Arts.", "museum_record": "https://www.artic.edu/artworks/80499", "inventory_number": "", "dimensions": "203.5 × 116.8 cm (80 1/8 × 46 in.)", "credit_line": "", "sources": ["https://www.artic.edu/artworks/80499", "https://artnap.com/artwork/aic-80499"], "check": "clean"}
