{"id": "aic-270002", "status": "ok", "meta": "Musical instruments in a bare corner of the drawing room at Strandgade 30: Vilhelm Hammershøi's Interior. The Music Room, 1907.", "about": "Musical instruments sit in a bare corner of a room, lit by soft light from a window outside the frame. Vilhelm Hammershøi moved to the apartment at Strandgade 30 in Copenhagen in 1898 and kept painting its rooms, sometimes with his wife Ida in them and sometimes without. The museum says he treated the furniture like stage props and shifted it around for looks, not use. Here nobody is there to play, and the museum reads the scene as silence. The brushstrokes are small and flickering.", "museum_record": "https://www.artic.edu/artworks/270002", "inventory_number": "", "dimensions": "70 × 59 cm (27 9/16 × 23 1/4 in.); Framed: 85.5 × 75.3 × 8.9 cm (33 5/8 × 29 5/8 × 3 1/2 in.)", "credit_line": "", "sources": ["https://www.artic.edu/artworks/270002", "https://artnap.com/artwork/aic-270002"], "check": "clean"}
