{"id": "si-saam_1980.137.93", "status": "ok", "meta": "Lexington, the Kentucky racehorse who sired more winners than any other American thoroughbred, painted by Thomas J. Scott in the 1850s.", "about": "Lexington, born in Kentucky in 1850, sired more winning racehorses than any other American thoroughbred, the museum says. Thomas J. Scott painted him in Kentucky when the horse was at his peak. Scott also wrote about him in a magazine. He gave the height as fifteen hands three inches and noted very wide shoulders and not an ounce of surplus. The museum points to the glossy coat and lean build, which the warm tones bring out.", "museum_record": "https://americanart.si.edu/collections/search/artwork/?id=22093", "inventory_number": "", "dimensions": "", "credit_line": "", "sources": ["https://americanart.si.edu/collections/search/artwork/?id=22093", "https://artnap.com/artwork/si-saam_1980.137.93"], "check": "clean"}
