{"id": "si-saam_1971.290", "status": "ok", "meta": "Golden light over trees and harvest fields in October, John Whetten Ehninger's 1860 landscape.", "about": "Golden light falls on trees and fields under soft clouds in John Whetten Ehninger's harvest scene. The museum says a picture of community, peace and plenty carried extra weight after the Civil War. It recalled a golden day when the nation was innocent and its fields had not been torn up by cannon fire. The museum also quotes a poem that calls back the past with pumpkin pie and the old days.", "museum_record": "https://americanart.si.edu/collections/search/artwork/?id=7943", "inventory_number": "", "dimensions": "", "credit_line": "", "sources": ["https://americanart.si.edu/collections/search/artwork/?id=7943", "https://artnap.com/artwork/si-saam_1971.290"], "check": "clean"}
