{"id": "cma-136276", "status": "ok", "meta": "An autumn twilight over the Grand Quai at Le Havre by Siebe Johannes ten Cate, who knew Kees van Dongen and Van Gogh.", "about": "Damp, chilly autumn twilight settles over the Grand Quai at Le Havre. Siebe Johannes ten Cate was born in Holland but spent most of his career in Paris. The museum says he briefly shared a Montmartre apartment with his friend Kees van Dongen and knew Vincent van Gogh. He was known for his pastels of harbors and cityscapes, and the museum calls this view melancholic.", "museum_record": "https://clevelandart.org/art/1960.166", "inventory_number": "", "dimensions": "", "credit_line": "", "sources": ["https://clevelandart.org/art/1960.166", "https://artnap.com/artwork/cma-136276"], "check": "clean"}
